1.2.0

Added 🚀
- Shared (Primitive, Array)
  - `default(value)` / `getDefault()` — set and retrieve fallback values for undefined inputs
  - `nullable()` / `nonNullable(message?)` — control whether null is accepted
  - `defined(message?)` / `optional()` / `notRequired()` — control whether undefined is accepted
  - `isValid(value)` / `isValidSync(value)` — boolean validation helpers (Promise<boolean> and boolean)
- String
  - `uuid(message?)` — UUID format validation (v1, v4, v5)
  - `length(size, message?)` — exact string length validation (alias for `exactLength()`)
- Array
  - `length(size, message?)` — exact array length validation
- Object
  - `pick(keys)` — create a new schema with only the selected fields
  - `omit(keys)` — create a new schema excluding the selected fields
  - `stripUnknown()` — remove unknown keys during validation instead of failing
  - `getDefault()` — collect defaults from child field schemas
  - `isValid(value)` / `isValidSync(value)` — boolean validation helpers

1.1.1

Fixes 🔨
- Fixed TypeScript declaration resolution under package.json `exports` for `moduleResolution: "bundler"` and `"node16"`
- ESM entrypoint now ships its own `.d.mts` declaration file (previously only CJS had declarations)
- Added `types` condition to `exports` map so TypeScript resolves types correctly for both `import` and `require`

Internal 🏡
- Enabled `dts: true` for the ESM build in tsup config
- Added `moduleResolution: "bundler"` regression test to `test-imports.js`

1.1.0

Internal 🏡 (Modernization - 2025)
- **Build System**: Replaced Rollup with tsup for 10-100x faster builds (~100ms vs several seconds)
- **Linting**: Upgraded ESLint from v8.57.1 to v9.39.2 with modern flat config
- **TypeScript**: Modernized configuration (ES2020 target, cleaned lib entries, added declarationMap)
- **CI/CD**: Consolidated to GitHub Actions (removed CircleCI), updated all actions to v4, Node 20 LTS
- **Dependencies**: Removed unused Rollup packages and tslib, added @eslint/js for ESLint 9
- **Testing**: Fixed Jest watchman warnings, updated test-imports to skip UMD format (no longer built)
- **Husky**: Updated to modern v9 syntax (removed deprecated install command)
- **Output Formats**: Removed UMD and AMD formats (modern npm packages only need CJS + ESM)

Breaking Changes ⚠️
- String & Number
  - `.min()` and `.max()` now use inclusive comparisons (matching Yup behavior)
    - `Nope.string().min(8).validate("password")` now passes (8 chars)
    - Previously required 9 characters for min(8)

Added 🚀
- New `test:imports` script to validate all import formats work correctly

Fixes 🔨
- Fixed build issues with rollup-plugin-typescript2/tslib compatibility
- Fixed TypeScript 5.7 strict type checking issues

